nds for R&amp;D show, for the first time, federal agency obligations to each of the individual U.S. territories. Data are from the Survey of Federal Funds for R&amp;D, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;05/06/2025&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25338&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25338&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2025.05.06&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;New Data on Federal Funding for R&amp;D to Individual U.S. Territories Available for the First Time for FY 2023&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2025&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reference&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:5238,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NCSES 25-215&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This document provides definitions of research and development (R&amp;D) from U.S. and international sources and by performing sector. By providing this resource, the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation aims to facilitate a better understanding of R&amp;D reporting requirements and improve the quality of R&amp;D data. R&amp;D definitions are provided unedited as they appear in their original sources.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/28/2025&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;ncses25215&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;ncses25215&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2025.04.28&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Definitions of Research and Development: An Annotated Compilation of Official Sources&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;New Construction&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Patenting and Trademark Activities&quot;,&quot;Product &amp; Business Process Innovation&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Publications &amp; Articles&quot;,&quot;Repairs and Renovations&quot;,&quot;State Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Technology Transfer Activities&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;,&quot;Work Activity&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2025&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoChart&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:5179,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-334&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The ratio of U.S. research and development (R&amp;D) to gross domestic product (GDP) reached 3.43% in 2022. The U.S. business-funded R&amp;D-to-GDP ratio climbed to 2.59% in 2022, with business funding 75% of domestic R&amp;D, compared to 31% in 1964. Federally funded R&amp;D was 0.63% of GDP and 18% of domestic R&amp;D in 2022 compared to 67% in 1964. Data are from the National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources series from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/24/2025&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25334&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25334&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2025.04.24&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Long-Term Trends Show Decline in Federally Funded R&amp;D as a Share of GDP while Business-Funded R&amp;D Share Increases&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2025&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoChart&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:5199,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-332&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Since 1951, the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics (NCSES) and its predecessors have provided annual data on the federal government’s obligations for research and development. During the past 75 years, these data have been witness to several historical events and changes. This InfoChart highlights several selected historical changes in the federal R&amp;D portfolio. Data are from the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development, conducted by NCSES, within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/10/2025&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25332&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25332&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2025.04.10&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;A Brief Annotated History of Federal R&amp;D Obligations: FYs 1951–2024&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2025&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Innovation and Global Competitiveness&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:5176,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-330&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;In 2021, 16.1% of companies reported pursuing design as a structured, creative process, which is similar to the minority of companies that reported product innovation between 2019 and 2021 (9.4%). This InfoBrief presents data from the 2022 Annual Business Survey (ABS) (data year 2021) on the design approaches used by U.S. businesses. The ABS is cosponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics (NCSES) within the U.S. National Science Foundation and by the Census Bureau. It collects data related to innovation, intellectual property, technology, and business owner characteristics from both microbusinesses and companies with 10 or more employees.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;03/24/2025&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25330&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25330&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2025.03.24&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The Different Approaches to Design by U.S. Businesses&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Product &amp; Business Process Innovation&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Work Activity&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2025&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:5137,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-328&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This set of data tables presents data on the research and development (R&amp;D) outlays and obligations of federal agencies. Outlays are provided by agency for total R&amp;D and total R&amp;D plant. Obligations are provided for R&amp;D by agency for type of work (basic research, applied research, and experimental development), field of R&amp;D (for basic research, applied research, and experimental development), type of performer, and geographic area. Obligations are provided for R&amp;D plant by agency for type of performer and geographic area. These data, collected by the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation, are the primary source of information about federal funding for R&amp;D in the United States.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;03/19/2025&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25328&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25328&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2025.03.19&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Funds for Research and Development: Fiscal Years 2023–24&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Amount of Research Space&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Disability Status&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2025&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:5156,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-329&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Federal obligations for research and experimental development decreased 2.1% in FY 2023. However, federal agency obligations for FY 2024 indicate federal funding for R&amp;D is estimated to increase by 5.0%. These data are from the latest edition of the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development, sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;03/19/2025&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25329&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25329&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2025.03.19&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Obligations Declined 2.1% in FY 2023; Estimated to Increase in FY 2024&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Sourc