240.2 million net assignable square feet (NASF) of science and engineering (S&amp;E) research space in FY 2023, an increase of 4 million NASF from FY 2021. Research space is a key component in the infrastructure that enabled $102 billion in higher education S&amp;E research in FY 2023. The reported increase in FY 2023 research space was the third lowest since FY 1990. The federal share of S&amp;E research space funding has been 3% or less since FYs 2016–17. These data are from the Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics (NCSES) within the U.S. National Science Foundation. &quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/17/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25318&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25318&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.12.17&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Research Space at Academic Institutions Totaled 240 Million Square Feet in FY 2023&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Amount of Research Space&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;New Construction&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Repairs and Renovations&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4836,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-310&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report contains data on the budget authority provided to U.S. federal agencies to fund the research and development (R&amp;D) and R&amp;D plant components of their programs in FYs 2023–25. FY 2023 numbers are final budget authority, FY 2024 numbers are preliminary and based on the annualized continuing resolution, FY 2025 numbers are from the president’s proposed budget. The tables in this report provide this budget authority detail, by agency and major programs, for each of the government budget functions in which R&amp;D is present. Several concluding tables also show budget authority data for R&amp;D in earlier years. Data were compiled by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/05/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25310&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25310&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.12.05&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function: Fiscal Years 2023–25&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Clinical Trials and Medical Projects&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoChart&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4876,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-311&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The FY 2025 proposed budget, when adjusted for inflation, requested $151 billion in budget authority for federal research and development (R&amp;D). A decrease of $7 billion from the inflation-adjusted $158 billion in actual budget authority for FY 2023 and preliminary FY 2024 amount. The National defense function decreased while other functions remained consistent. Data are from the Federal Funding for R&amp;D, by Budget Function, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/05/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25311&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25311&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.12.05&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Inflation-Adjusted Federal Budget Authority for R&amp;D Totals $151 Billion in FY 2025 Proposed Budget&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Doctorate Recipients from U.S. Universities&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Doctorate Recipients from U.S. Universities&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4757,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-300&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report summarizes trends in U.S. doctoral education by using data from the 2023 Survey of Earned Doctorates, an annual census of research doctorate recipients from U.S. universities. Important trends in this population are highlighted in this report, including the representation of women, minorities, and temporary visa holders; fields that are attracting graduate students; employment opportunities after graduation; 