uot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;,&quot;Work Activity&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4756,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 25-302&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This InfoBrief presents research and development (R&amp;D) data on microbusinesses (businesses with one to nine domestic employees). In 2022, microbusinesses reported a total of $7.6 billion in R&amp;D costs, of which 88%, or $6.7 billion, was domestic and 75%, or $5.7 billion, was performed by the microbusinesses themselves. R&amp;D costs include the amount that businesses spent of their own money and from other sources on R&amp;D they perform, as well as the amount they paid others to perform R&amp;D. Data are from the Annual Business Survey, developed and cosponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation and by the Census Bureau.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;10/29/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf25302&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf25302&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.10.29&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Microbusinesses Performed $5.7 billion of R&amp;D in the United States in 2022&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Patenting and Trademark Activities&quot;,&quot;Product &amp; Business Process Innovation&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;,&quot;Work Activity&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Workforce&quot;,&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Postdoctorates at Federally Funded R&amp;D Centers&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Postdoctorates at Federally Funded R&amp;D Centers&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4726,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-339&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Federally funded research and development centers (FFRDCs) in the United States supply researchers with the facilities and resources needed to conduct critical studies in science, engineering, and health. Between 2021 and 2023, the number of postdocs receiving training at FFRDCs remained stable, with 3,629 postdocs reported in 2023 and 3,637 reported  in 2021. Between 2019 and 2023, the number of postdocs who were U.S. citizens or permanent residents increased by 190 (13% increase), whereas the number of postdocs with temporary visas increased by 104 (5% increase), resulting in a partial recovery of the decline in percentage of temporary visa holder postdocs in 2021. Data are from the 2023 Survey of Postdocs at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers, sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation and by the National Institutes of Health.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;10/15/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24339&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24339&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.10.15&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Postdocs at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Postdocs at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Ongoing Changes in the Demographic Composition of Postdoctoral Researchers at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers: 2023&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Citizenship&quot;,&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Postdoctorates&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Workforce&quot;,&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Postdoctorates at Federally Funded R&amp;D Centers&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Postdoctorates at Federally Funded R&amp;D Centers&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4652,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-333&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The detailed tables in this report contain aggregate counts of postdocs at federally funded research and development centers (FFRDCs), by citizenship, ethnicity, race, sex, source of financial support, and field of research. Data are from the Survey of Postdocs at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers, which is the primary source of information on postdocs employed in FFRDCs in the United States. The survey is sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation and by the National Institutes of Health.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;10/15/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24333&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24333&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.10.15&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Postdocs at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Postdocs at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Postdocs at Federally Funded Research and Development Centers: Fall 2023&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;Citizenship&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Postdoctorates&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4698,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-338&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;These tables present the results of the Nonprofit Research Activities FY 2022 module of the 2023 Annual Business Survey, conducted by the Census Bureau for the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation. It is the third collection of nonprofit R&amp;D data by the Annual Business Survey and the continuation of an annual data series for this population. These data are the primary source of information about tax-exempt nonprofit organizations’ R&amp;D performance and funding in the United States.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;10/08/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24338&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24338&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.10.08&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities (NPRA) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities (NPRA) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities: FY 2022&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Employment Status&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4676,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-337&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;U.S. nonprofit organizations spent an estimated $28.1 billion on research and experimental development (R&amp;D) performed within their organizations in FY 2022, an increase of 4% in current dollars from FY 2021. The largest funding source was the federal government, contributing $11.6 billion, or 42%, of the total. Data are from the Nonprofit Research Activities (NPRA) FY 2022 module of the 2023 Annual Business Survey, conducted by the Census Bureau for the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation. The FY 2022 cycle contains the first data on capital expenditures research operations within nonprofit organizations. These expenditures are for capital purchases related to R&amp;D activities—such as land acquisition, capitalized software, and major machinery and equipment. In FY 2022, nonprofits spent $972 million on such capital purchases, the largest proportion of which was for major machinery and equipment.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;10/08/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24337&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24337&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.10.08&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities (NPRA) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities (NPRA) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;U.S. Nonprofits Spent $28 Billion on R&amp;D Activities in FY 2022&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4696,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-335&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The tables in this report present data from the Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey. The BERD Survey is the primary source of information on domestic and global research and development (R&amp;D) expenditures and the R&amp;D workforce for companies with 10 or more employees operating in the 50 U.S. states and the District of Columbia. The survey is conducted annually by the Census Bureau in accordance with an interagency agreement with the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation. These data are used by government agencies, corporations, research organizations, and academics to assess trends in the performance and funding of R&amp;D.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/30/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24335&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24335&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.09.30&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development: 2022&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Employment Status&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Degrees&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Patenting and Trademark Activities&quot;,&quot;Product &amp; Business Process Innovation&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Skilled Technical Workforce&quot;,&quot;Technology Transfer Activities&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental developm