cation Degrees&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Directorate Profiles&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Profiles of the National Science Foundation Directorates&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Profiles of the National Science Foundation Directorates&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4720,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NCSES 24-210&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:null,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/26/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;ncses24210&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;ncses24210&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.09.26&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Directorate for STEM Education (EDU)&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Degrees&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reference&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Profiles of the National Science Foundation Directorates&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Profiles of the National Science Foundation Directorates&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4717,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NCSES 24-215&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The Directorate Profiles from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation (NSF) provide visualizations on research doctorate recipients from U.S. institutions, by NSF Directorate. This reference document provides additional methodology information for the graphics in the 7 profiles, as well as tabular versions of the data used.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/26/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;ncses24215&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;ncses24215&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.09.26&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Directorate Profiles: Technical Notes&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Citizenship&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Degrees&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Income and Salary&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Postgraduation Plans&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Student Loan Debt&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Doctorate Recipients from U.S. Universities&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Doctorate Recipients from U.S. Universities&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4654,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-336&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;These tables release data from the 2023 Survey of Earned Doctorates (SED), an annual census of research doctorate recipients from U.S. universities. The tables include long-term trend data on doctorate recipients by field; educational pathways to the doctorate and sources of financial support; postgraduation employment plans; and representation of women, minorities, and temporary visa holders among doctorate recipients. Data also will be available in an interactive data tool (https://ncsesdata.nsf.gov/builder/sed) and the Restricted Data Analysis System (https://ncsesdata.nsf.gov/rdas/). The SED is sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation and by three other federal agencies: the National Institutes of Health, Department of Education, and National Endowment for the Humanities.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/24/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24336&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24336&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.09.24&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Earned Doctorates (SED)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Earned Doctorates (SED)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Doctorate Recipients from U.S. Universities: 2023 Data Tables&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Citizenship&quot;,&quot;Disability Status&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Faculty Rank, Tenure Status&quot;,&quot;Family Characteristics&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Financial Support&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Degrees&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Income and Salary&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Postdoctorates&quot;,&quot;Postgraduation Plans&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Student Loan Debt&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBytes&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4632,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NCSES 24-206&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Latest visualizations from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics using data from the Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering 2017–22 on full-time master’s student enrollment by sex, citizenship, and field of study.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/04/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;ncses24206&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;ncses24206&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.09.04&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Full-Time Master’s Student Enrollment in Science, Engineering, and Health&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Enrollment&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4592,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-332&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;At the turn of the century, the federal government funded approximately 60% of basic research. In 2022, the federal government is estimated to fund about 40% of basic research among all U.S. domestic performers of R&amp;D. At the same time, federal budget authority and federal obligations for basic research as a share of total federal R&amp;D are among the highest levels they have been. This InfoBrief provides perspective on this dichotomy and provides data users with an understanding of federal funding for basic research as part of the overall national portfolio of R&amp;D performance and within the federal R&amp;D enterprise. Data are from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;08/15/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24332&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24332&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.08.15&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Analysis of Federal Funding for Research and Development in 2022: Basic Research&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4532,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-331&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Federal government funding for science and engineering support to higher education goes to a select few institutions. For example, in FY 2022, out of nearly 1,100 institutions subject to federal obligations, 100 accounted for 80% of all federal S&amp;E support. This InfoBrief will provide data users with information on the federal government’s science and engineering support to various types of minority-serving institutions. Estimates are from the FY 2022 Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;07/22/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24331&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24331&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.07.22&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;FY 2022 Federal Science and Engineering Support to Selected Types of Minority-Serving Institutions&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4512,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-330&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The nation’s 42 federally funded research and development centers (FFRDCs) spent $29.3 billion on research and development (R&amp;D) in FY 2023, an annual increase of 12.7% in current dollars. The federal government funded $28.9 billion of the R&amp;D total, which represented a 12.8% increase in federal support to FFRDCs. These and the other statistics in this report come from the FY 2023 FFRDC Research and Development Survey, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;07/15/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24330&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24330&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.07.15&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;FFRDC Research and Development Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;FFRDC Research and Development Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federally Funded R&amp;D Centers Report 13% Increase in R&amp;D Spending in FY 2023&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4452,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-328&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;These data tables provide data on research and development (R&amp;D) expenditures for federally funded research and development centers (FFRDCs). Expenditures data are displayed for individually named FFRDCs, by source of funding, and type of R&amp;D. Data are from the FY 2023 FFRDC Research and Development Survey, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;07/15/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24328&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24328&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.07.15&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;FFRDC Research and Development Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;FFRDC Research and Development Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;FFRDC Research and Development Expenditures: Fiscal Year 2023&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Innovation and Global Competitiveness&quot;,&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoChart&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4492,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-329&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;U.S. research and development (R&amp;D) performed by the semiconductor and other electronic components manufacturing industry (NAICS 3344) reached $47.4 billion in 2021, an increase of 9.8% from 2020 in current dollars. Of this amount, $45.5 billion was R&amp;D paid for and performed by the company. California performed by far the most company-funded U.S. semiconductor business R&amp;D among states at $23 billion, or 51% of total. Data are from the Business Enterprise Research and Development Survey, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics and the Census Bureau.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;07/09/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24329&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24329&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.07.09&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Six States Perform Around 90% of Semiconductor Business R&amp;D, Led by California&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4472,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-327&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;In FY 2022, federal contracts for research and experimental development (R&amp;D) totaled $51.9 billion, whereas federal grants for R&amp;D totaled $52.4 billion. Federal contracts for R&amp;D plant totaled $1.0 billion, whereas federal grants for R&amp;D plant totaled $626 million. These data are from the latest edition of the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development, sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;07/01/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24327&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24327&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.07.01&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Obligations for R&amp;D Contracts Increase 1.8% in FY 2022; Obligations for R&amp;D Grants Increase 2.7%&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Workforce&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBytes&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4413,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NCSES 24-205&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Latest visualizations from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics using data from the Survey of Earned Doctorates 2022 on definite commitments to accept new employment or return to predoctoral employment, excluding postdoctoral study.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;06/17/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;ncses24205&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;ncses24205&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.06.17&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Earned Doctorates (SED)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Earned Doctorates (SED)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Sector of Employment of S&amp;E Doctorate Recipients with Definite U.S. Commitments&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Postgraduation Plans&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4372,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-325&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;In FY 2022, federal agency obligations to universities and colleges for science and engineering (S&amp;E) activities increased 3% from FY 2021 to a historical high of nearly $45 billion. S&amp;E activities include research and development (R&amp;D); R&amp;D plant; facilities and equipment for instruction in S&amp;E; fellowships, traineeships, and training grants; and other general support for S&amp;E. Estimates are from the FY 2022 Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support module within the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;06/10/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24325&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24325&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.06.10&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Science and Engineering Support for Academic Institutions Increased 3% in FY 2022; Support to HBCUs Increased 19%&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Financial Support&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Repairs and Renovations&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4392,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-326&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;These tables present FY 2022 data on federal direct support of higher education and nonprofit institutions&#39; research and development. Data include science and engineering support by type of activity, as well as ranking by state, agency, and individual institution. Data are from the Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation. This survey is the only source of comprehensive data on federal science and engineering funding to individual academic and nonprofit institutions.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;06/10/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24326&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24326&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.06.10&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions: Fiscal Year 2022&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Financial Support&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Workforce&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4071,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSB-2024-5&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) workers make important contributions to improve the nation&#39;s living standards, economic growth, and global competitiveness. This report touches on the size, growth, education, salary, and diversity of the STEM workforce. STEM occupations cover a diverse range of opportunities, including those not typically considered STEM (e.g., mechanics, electricians, and carpenters). More than 36 million people work in STEM occupations, of which more than half did not have a bachelor&#39;s degree. In addition, workers in STEM occupations have higher employment rates and higher median earnings than their non-STEM counterparts.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;05/30/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsb20245&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsb20245&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.05.30&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The STEM Labor Force: Scientists, Engineers, and Skilled Technical Workers&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Interactive&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:5816,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Updated data for Science and Engineering State Profiles are now available. This product provides state-level rankings and totals of science and engineering data for the 50 states, District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico. The data tool allows users to compare state profiles for up to seven states or download the entire data set. Science and Engineering State Profiles is produced by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics of the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;05/23/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/states/download/state-profiles-2024-05.xlsx&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf00000&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.05.23&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles: Spring 2024 Update&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4092,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSB-2024-6&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Investment in research and development (R&amp;D) is essential for a country’s success in the global economy and for its ability to address challenges and opportunities. R&amp;D contributes to innovation and competitiveness. In 2021, the business sector was the leading performer and funder of U.S. R&amp;D. The federal government was the second-largest overall funding source and the largest funding source for U.S. basic research; the higher education sector was the largest performer of basic research. Based on internationally comparable estimates, the United States had the highest R&amp;D expenditures in 2021, followed by China, Japan, and Germany. &quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;05/21/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsb20246&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsb20246&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.05.21&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Research and Development: U.S. Trends and International Comparisons&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoChart&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4352,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-324&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;FY 2022 total federal obligations for research and development increased 0.4% from FY 2021, and preliminary FY 2023 obligations are expected to decrease 2.1%. However, when adjusted for inflation FY 2022 obligations decreased 6.1% from FY 2021, and preliminary FY 2023 obligations are expected to decrease an additional 6.4% from FY 2022. Data are from the Survey of Federal Funds for R&amp;D, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the U.S. National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;05/20/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24324&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24324&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.05.20&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Inflation-Adjusted Federal R&amp;D Obligations Expected to Decline for Second Year from FY 2021 High&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Innovation and Global Competitiveness&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3788,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSB-2024-7&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Knowledge- and technology-intensive (KTI) industries are those with high and medium-high R&amp;D intensity. They include 10 manufacturing and 3 services industries. This report discusses U.S. and global KTI production patterns and international trade. The report shows that KTI industries value added account for about a 10th of U.S. GDP. In 2022, China and the United States were the top two producers of KTI output, each representing over a quarter of global KTI value added. And China has been the leading KTI manufacturing exporter since 2008. In 2022, the United States and Germany were the next largest KTI goods exporters.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/22/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsb20247&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsb20247&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.04.22&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Production and Trade of Knowledge- and Technology-Intensive Industries&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Innovation and Global Competitiveness&quot;,&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4313,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-323&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Artificial intelligence (AI) and COVID-19 research are two areas that have complex challenges that both domestic and international institutions are motivated to overcome. A concentration on domestic research can indicate the presence of sufficient domestic knowledge and resources or an interest in preserving in-house expertise. This InfoBrief examines the extent to which top producers of science and engineering articles engaged in domestic and international collaborations in AI and COVID-19 research.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/11/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24323&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24323&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.04.11&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;International Collaboration in Selected Critical and Emerging Fields: COVID and Artificial Intelligence&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Attitudes About Science&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Publications &amp; Articles&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4293,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-321&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This set of data tables present data on the research and development (R&amp;D) outlays and obligations of federal agencies. Outlays are provided by agency for total R&amp;D and total R&amp;D plant. Obligations are provided for R&amp;D by agency for type of work (basic research, applied research, and experimental development), field of R&amp;D (for basic research, applied research, and experimental development), type of performer, and geographic area. Obligations are provided for R&amp;D plant by agency for type of performer and geographic area. These data, collected by the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics, are the primary source of information about federal funding for R&amp;D in the United States.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/03/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24321&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24321&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.04.03&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Funds for Research and Development: Fiscal Years 2022–23&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Disability Status&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;State Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4312,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-322&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Federal obligations for research and experimental development were virtually unchanged in FY 2022, increasing 0.4% from FY 2021. However, federal agency obligations for FY 2023 indicate federal funding for R&amp;D is estimated to decline by more than 2%. These data are from the latest edition of the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development, sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/03/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24322&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24322&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.04.03&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Obligations Increased 0.4% in FY 2022; Estimated to Decline in FY 2023&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4253,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-320&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Between 2021 and 2022, graduate student enrollment in science, engineering, and health (SEH) fields increased by 5.0% (up 38,378 students), mostly due to an increase of 42,816 temporary visa holders enrolled in full-time master’s programs. Full-time SEH master’s enrollment in 2022 was 319,618, whereas full-time doctoral enrollment was 259,683, the highest number recorded in the Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS). These and other findings in this InfoBrief are from the 2022 GSS, which is sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation and by the National Institutes of Health.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;03/20/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24320&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24320&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.03.20&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Graduate Enrollment in Science, Engineering, and Health Continues to Increase among Foreign Nationals, while Postdoctoral Appointment Trends Vary across Fields&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Attitudes About Science&quot;,&quot;Citizenship&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Degrees&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Enrollment&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Non-faculty Research Personnel&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Postdoctorates&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Work-related Training&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Workforce&quot;,&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4232,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-319&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report presents data from the 2022 Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering, sponsored by National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation and by the National Institutes of Health. The tables show trends within science, engineering, and selected health fields on graduate student enrollment, postdoc appointments, and doctorate-holding nonfaculty researchers, as well as counts by selected characteristics, such as sex, ethnicity, race, citizenship, field of study, and source of financial support.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;03/20/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24319&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24319&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.03.20&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering: Fall 2022&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Citizenship&quot;,&quot;Clinical Trials and Medical Projects&quot;,&quot;Disability Status&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Financial Support&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Degrees&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Enrollment&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Non-faculty Research Personnel&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Postdoctorates&quot;,&quot;Postgraduation Plans&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Work-related Training&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4111,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSB-2024-3&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The global competitiveness of the United States is supported through the nation’s STEM talent, R&amp;D-driven discovery, and translation of knowledge into the economy and society through innovation. The United States is the largest performer of R&amp;D, but the overall balance of global science and engineering (S&amp;E) resources and activity continues a long-term shift toward other areas of the world. The United States is distinguished by the strength of U.S. universities as destinations for international students, its highly cited and collaborative S&amp;E research, and its leadership in high-technology services.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;03/13/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsb20243&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsb20243&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.03.13&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The State of U.S. Science and Engineering 2024&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Innovation and Global Competitiveness&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3687,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSB-2024-1&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The practical application of science and technology starts with invention and leads to innovation, job creation, and new business formation. Every sector, including governments and universities, plays an important part in these activities through knowledge transfer activities. This thematic report provides patent data by technology area and geography to illustrate trends in invention in the United States and internationally. Relevant data on trademarks are also presented. In addition, indicators are included that measure the transfer of knowledge and technologies from federal agencies and universities to businesses. Trends in the financing of innovation are presented through data on federal funding for small businesses and venture capital investments.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/29/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsb20241&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsb20241&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.02.29&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Invention, Knowledge Transfer, and Innovation&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reference&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:5776,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The Master Government list of Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDCs), maintained by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics of the National Science Foundation, has been updated for 2024. FFRDCs are listed by sponsoring agency, administrator type, location, and type of activity.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/20/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://ncses.nsf.gov/resource/master-gov-lists-ffrdc/prior-lists&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf00000&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.02.20&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Master Government List of Federally Funded R&amp;D Centers: FY 2024&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;STEM Education&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3727,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSB-2024-4&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report describes confidence in science, understanding of scientific research and new topics such as neurotechnology and artificial intelligence, and engagement with science through media and scientific activities. The majority of U.S. adults—77% as of September 2022—express at least a fair amount of confidence in scientists to act in the public interest. Evidence also suggests perceptions of new science and technology topics may change as experiences grow. U.S. adults with greater understanding of scientific logic tend to express more trust in scientists to act in society’s best interests than do those with less understanding.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/14/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsb20244&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsb20244&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.02.14&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Technology: Public Perceptions, Awareness, and Information Sources&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4172,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-316&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;In FY 2021, federal agency obligations to universities and colleges for science and engineering (S&amp;E) activities increased to a historical high of nearly $43 billion, up 10.5% from FY 2020. S&amp;E activities include research and development (R&amp;D); R&amp;D plant; facilities and equipment for instruction in S&amp;E; fellowships, traineeships, and training grants; and other general support for S&amp;E. Estimates are from the FY 2021 Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;01/29/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24316&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24316&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.01.29&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Science and Engineering Support to Higher Education Increased 10% in FY 2021&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Clinical Trials and Medical Projects&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:4153,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-311&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions is a congressionally mandated census completed by federal agencies that obligated money in the survey year for direct support of higher education and nonprofit institutions&#39; research and development. The Federal S&amp;E Support Survey is the only source of comprehensive data on federal science and engineering funding to individual academic and nonprofit institutions. As of the FY 2021 data collection, the survey was incorporated as the Federal Science and Engineering Support module within the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;01/29/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24311&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24311&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.01.29&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Science and Engineering Support to Universities, Colleges, and Nonprofit Institutions: Fiscal Year 2021&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Financial Support&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Skilled Technical Workforce&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4154,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-310&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report contains data on the budget authority provided to U.S. federal agencies to fund the research and development (R&amp;D) and R&amp;D plant components of their programs in FYs 2022–24. The tables in this report provide this budget authority detail by agency and major programs for each of the governmental functions in which R&amp;D is present. Several concluding tables also show budget authority data for R&amp;D in earlier years. Data were compiled by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;01/25/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24310&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24310&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.01.25&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function: Fiscal Years 2022–24&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;Clinical Trials and Medical Projects&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBytes&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4173,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NCSES 24-204&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Latest visualizations from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics using data from the Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function FYs 2022–24 on federal budget authority for R&amp;D and R&amp;D plant by governmental functions (e.g., agriculture, energy, health, national defense).&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;01/25/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;ncses24204&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;ncses24204&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.01.25&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding, by Budget Function: FYs 2022–24&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4174,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-318&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report provides current data on the levels of and key trends in the performance and funding of research and development (R&amp;D) in the United States, with comparisons to the historical record (back to 1953). Detailed statistical tables present data on U.S. R&amp;D expenditures by performing sector, source of funds, type of R&amp;D, and state. Data are drawn from multiple surveys from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;01/22/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24318&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24318&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.01.22&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources: 2021–22 Data Update&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;State Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;National Patterns of R&amp;D Resources&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:4175,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 24-317&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;New data from the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics (NCSES) within the National Science Foundation indicate that research and experimental development (R&amp;D) performed in the United States totaled $789.1 billion in 2021. The estimated total for 2022, based on performer-reported expectations, is $885.6 billion. The ratio of U.S. R&amp;D to GDP was 3.34% in 2020, exceeding the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development average of 2.72%.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;01/22/2024&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf24317&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf24317&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2024.01.22&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;U.S. R&amp;D Increased by $72 Billion in 2021 to $789 Billion; Estimate for 2022 Indicates Further Increase to $886 Billion&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;State Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2024&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;