uot;NSF 23-310&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;A quarter (25%) of the estimated 4.9 million for-profit companies with at least one employee introduced an innovation during 2017–19. Eleven percent of these companies introduced one or more product innovations, and 22% introduced one or more business process innovations. Data are from the Annual Business Survey (ABS), which provides a comprehensive view of business innovation in the United States. The ABS was developed and is cosponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation and by the Census Bureau.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/28/2022&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf23310&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf23310&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2022.12.28&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Innovation Data from the 2020 Annual Business Survey&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Patenting and Trademark Activities&quot;,&quot;Product &amp; Business Process Innovation&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Skilled Technical Workforce&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2022&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:3048,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 23-317&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;These tables present the results of the Nonprofit Research Activities FY 2020 module of the 2021 Annual Business Survey, conducted by the Census Bureau for the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation. It is the first collection of nonprofit R&amp;D data by the Annual Business Survey and the beginning of an annual data series for this population. This survey is the primary source of information about 501(c) nonprofit organizations’ R&amp;D performance and funding in the United States.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/28/2022&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf23317&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf23317&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2022.12.28&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities (NPRA) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities (NPRA) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Nonprofit Research Activities: FY 2020&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Employment Status&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Nonprofit R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Agreement (contract, grant, reimbursement, etc.)&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2022&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:3047,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 23-316&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;U.S. nonprofits performed an estimated $28.0 billion on research and development (R&amp;D) in FY 2020, 4% of the estimated total R&amp;D performance in the United States in 2020. The largest funding source for nonprofit R&amp;D performance was the federal government, contributing $12.3 billion. Nonprofit or