ederal increase since FY 2011, when the American Recovery and Reinvestment Act of 2009 supplemented the flow of R&amp;D support dollars. The data discussed in this report are from the Higher Education Research and Development Survey, sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation. &quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/15/2022&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf23303&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf23303&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2022.12.15&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Higher Education Research and Development (HERD) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Higher Education Research and Development (HERD) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Universities Report Largest Growth in Federally Funded R&amp;D Expenditures since FY 2011&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Clinical Trials and Medical Projects&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2022&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:2966,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 23-308&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;U.S. research-performing universities and colleges reported over 236 million net assignable square feet (NASF) of science and engineering (S&amp;E) research space in FY 2021. This total represents an increase of more than 9 million NASF since FY 2019 and 34 million NASF since FY 2011. Research space is a key component in the infrastructure that enabled U.S. colleges and universities to conduct almost $85 billion in S&amp;E research in FY 2021. The data discussed in this report are from the biennial Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics (NCSES) within the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/15/2022&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf23308&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf23308&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2022.12.15&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;University Science and Engineering Research Space Increased More Than 30 Million Square Feet in the Past Decade&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Amount of Research Space&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Institutions&quot;,&quot;New Construction&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;Repairs and Renovations&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2022&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Innovation and Global Competitiveness&quot;,&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:2985,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 23-313&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The detailed tables in this report present data from the 2021 Annual Business Survey (ABS) (data year 2020). The ABS is the primary source of data on research and development of for-profit, nonfarm businesses with one to nine employees operating in the 50 U.S. states and the District of Columbia. The ABS also collects data on innovation, technology, intellectual property, and business owner characteristics of business of all sizes. The 2021 ABS is the fourth year of the ABS. The survey is conducted annually by the Census Bureau for the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation. &quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/14/2022&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf23313&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf23313&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2022.12.14&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Annual Business Survey: 2021 (Data Year 2020)&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;COVID-19 Pandemic Impacts&quot;,&quot;Employment Status&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Knowledge and Technology Intensive (KTI) Industries&quot;,&quot;Minorities in Higher Education&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Product &amp; Business Process Innovation&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;Race and Ethnicity&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Skilled Technical Workforce&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;,&quot;Work Activity&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2022&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:2865,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 23-305&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This InfoBrief presents research and development and other data on microbusinesses (those with one to nine domestic employees), by industry, funding source, type of R&amp;D, and state. In 2020, microbusinesses reported $6.7 billion in R&amp;D expenditures or costs in the United State, $5.6 billion of which was performed by the microbusinesses themselves. This InfoBrief distinguishes between all R&amp;D costs and R&amp;D performance costs, which are the costs only for R&amp;D performed by the business. Data for this InfoBrief are from the Annual Business Survey (ABS), developed and cosponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation and by the Census Bureau.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/14/2022&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf23305&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf23305&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2022.12.14&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Annual Business Survey (ABS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Microbusinesses Performed $5.6 Billion of R&amp;D in the United States in 2020&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Employment Sector&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Patenting and Trademark Activities&quot;,&quot;Product &amp; Business Process Innovation&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Intensity&quot;,&quot;Sex&quot;,&quot;Type of R&amp;D (basic, applied, experimental development)&quot;],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2022&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:2885,&