active&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:5514,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Updated data for Science and Engineering State Profiles are now available. This product provides state-level rankings and totals of science and engineering data for the 50 states, District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico. The data tool allows users to compare state profiles for up to seven states or download the entire data set. Science and Engineering State Profiles is produced by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics of the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;11/22/2021&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/states/download/state-profiles-2021-11.xlsx&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf00000&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2021.11.22&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles: Fall 2021 Update&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Research and Development Funding and Performance&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:1744,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 22-303&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The Business Enterprise Research and Development Survey (BERD), cosponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics (NCSES) within the National Science Foundation (NSF) and by the U.S. Census Bureau, is an annual business R&amp;D survey that offers international comparability and succeeds the Business Research and Development Survey (BRDS, 2017–18), the Business R&amp;D and Innovation Survey (BRDIS, 2008–16), and the Survey of Industrial Research and Development (SIRD, 1953–2007). Using data from BERD, this InfoBrief shows that businesses spent $493 billion on R&amp;D performance in 2019, with $429 funding from companies’ own sources and $64 billion from other sources. These amounts reflect the second year of double-digit growth in the level of national domestic R&amp;D performance, and this robust performance seems likely to continue in 2020, based on the large increase in funding that companies planned to spend from their own funds for domestic R&amp;D performance. &quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;11/18/2021&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;nsf22303&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf22303&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2021.11.18&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Businesses Reported an 11.8% Increase to Nearly a Half Trillion Dollars for U.S. R&amp;D Performance During 2019&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;By Country&quot;,&quot;By State or Region&quot;,&quot;Citizenship&quot;,&quot;Faculty Rank, Tenure Status&quot;,&quot;Federal Government/Agency R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Federally Funded Research and Development Centers (FFRDC) R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;Fields of Study&quot;,&quot;Financial Support&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Degrees&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Enrollment&quot;,&quot;Higher Education R&amp;D&quot;,&quot;New Construction&quot;,&quot;Occupation&quot;,&quot;Production and Value Added&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Capital Expenditures&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Cost Type&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Employment&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding by Government&quot;,&quot;R&amp;D Funding Source&quot