ate and department or agency. These data were collected by the Survey of State Government Research and Development, conducted by the U.S. Census Bureau for the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;11/20/2019&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://ncsesdata.nsf.gov/sgrd/2018/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf00000&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2019.11.20&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of State Government Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of State Government Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of State Government Research and Development: FY 2018&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Higher Education Research and Development (HERD)&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Higher Education Research and Development (HERD)&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:5333,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 20-302&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Funding of higher education research and development increased across all funding sources in FY 2018, marking the third straight year of steady growth. Total R&amp;D expenditures increased $4.1 billion (5.5%) from FY 2017, reaching $79.4 billion. Federal funding of R&amp;D has increased in both current and constant dollars for three straight years, according to data from the Higher Education Research and Development (HERD) Survey by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;11/13/2019&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/2020/nsf20302/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf2030