ources was $339 billion in 2017, a 6.7% increase from 2016. Funding from other sources was $61 billion in 2017 and $57 billion in 2016. Data are from the Business R&amp;D and Innovation Survey and Business Research and Development Survey, both developed and cosponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation and by the U.S. Census Bureau.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/26/2019&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/2019/nsf19326/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf19326&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2019.09.26&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;,&quot;Business Research and Development Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;},{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Research and Development Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business R&amp;D Performance in the United States Reached $400 Billion in 2017, a 6.8% Increase from 2016&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Workforce&quot;],&quot;archived&quot;:false,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Reports&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering Indicators&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:405,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSB-2019-8&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The science and engineering (S&amp;E) labor force helps to create and advance our scientific and technological knowledge, transform these advances into goods and services, and fuel America’s economy, security, and quality of life. This report details several aspects of the U.S. S&amp;E workforce, including growth, demographic makeup, earnings, and 