cientists and Engineers with U.S. Doctorates&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:5259,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 19-307&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;In 2017, an estimated 1,103,200 individuals worldwide held a research doctoral degree in a science, engineering, or health (SEH) field that was earned at a U.S. academic institution. Currently, 35% of the U.S.-trained SEH doctorate holders residing and working in the United States are women, compared with 23% 20 years ago. The number of these women has more than doubled during this period, rising to 287,250 in 2017. Findings are from the 2017 Survey of Doctorate Recipients, conducted by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation and by the National Institutes of Health.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/12/2019&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/2019/nsf19307/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf19307&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2019.02.12&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Doctorate Recipients (SDR)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Doctorate Recipients (SDR)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Number of Women with U.S. Doctorates in Science, Engineering, or Health Employed in the United States More Than Doubles since 1997&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Characteristics of Scientists and Engineers with U.S. Doctorates&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Characteristics of Scientists and Engineers with U.S. Doctorates&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:5228,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Tables from the 2017 Survey of Doctorate Recipients (SDR) present data on the demographic characteristics, labor force status, occupations, employment sector, and median annual salaries of individuals with a U.S. research doctoral degree in a science, engineering, or health field. The SDR is sponsored by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics within the National Science Foundation and by the National Institutes of Health.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/12/2019&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://ncsesdata.nsf.gov/doctoratework/2017/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf00000&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2019.02.12&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Doctorate Recipients (SDR)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Doctorate Recipients (SDR)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Doctorate Recipients, 2017&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Interactive&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:5266,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Updated data for Science and Engineering State Profiles are now available. This product provides state-level rankings and totals of science and engineering data for the 50 states, District of Columbia, and Puerto Rico. The data tool allows users to compare state profiles for up to seven states or download the entire data set. Science and Engineering State Profiles is produced by the National Center for Science and Engineering Statistics of the National Science Foundation.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;12/21/2018&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/states/download/state-profiles-2018-12.xlsx&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf00000&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2018.12