TO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Women, Minorities, and Persons with Disabilities in STEM&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3777,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 07-315&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report continues a series of Congressionally-mandated biennial reports, providing data on the participation of women, minorities, and persons with disabilities in science and engineering education and employment. The data and analyses presented here can be used to track progress, inform the development of policies to increase participation in science and engineering, and evaluate the effectiveness of such policies.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;03/05/2007&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/wmpd/archives/wmpd_2007.zip&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf07315&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2007.03.05&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Women, Minorities, and Persons with Disabilities in S&amp;E: 2007&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2007&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business and Industry R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:2488,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 07-314&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report will present all of the statistics produced from the 2003 cycle of the Survey of Industrial Research and Development by size of company, the sources of R&amp;D funds, character of R&amp;D, and industry using the North American Industrial Classification System (NAICS).  Also included will be tables covering historical trends in R&amp;D; R&amp;D as a percent of sales; employment and cost of R&amp;D scientists and engineers; and R&amp;D statistics by state.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/26/2007&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/nsf07314/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf07314&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2007.02.26&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D and Innovation Survey (BRDIS)&quot;,&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business R&amp;D and Innovation Survey (BRDIS)&quot;},{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Research and Development in Industry: 2003&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2007&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;International Investment and R&amp;D Data Link&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;International Investment and R&amp;D Data Link&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3675,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 07-310&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This federal data-sharing project, the first undertaken under the Confidential Information Protection and Statistical Efficiency Act of 2002, linked company-specific data from the Survey of Industrial Research and Development with international data on U.S. multinational corporations (MNCs) and U.S. affiliates of foreign MNCs. Among other benefits, the linked data set provided first-time information on R&amp;D activities of MNCs, allowed improvements in sample design for the surveys used, and provided useful data quality information.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/08/2007&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/infbrief/nsf07310/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf07310&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2007.02.08&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Linking Multinational Corporations Data from International Investment Surveys and Industrial R&amp;D Surveys&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2007&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:1843,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 07-313&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;A revised methodology for classifying companies into industries for the Survey of Industrial Research and Development adjusts for business conducted overseas, outsourcing, startup R&amp;D efforts, and other scenarios. The new methodology resulted in a 40% increase in the amount of R&amp;D classified as manufacturing in 2004. The largest adjustment in manufacturing industries was in pharmaceuticals and medicines. Decreases in nonmanufacturing were concentrated in wholesale trade, company/enterprise management, and scientific R&amp;D services.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/07/2007&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/infbrief/nsf07313/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf07313&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2007.02.07&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Business R&amp;D and Innovation Survey (BRDIS)&quot;,&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business R&amp;D and Innovation Survey (BRDIS)&quot;},{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Business Enterprise Research and Development (BERD) Survey&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Revised Industry Classification Better Reflects Structure of Business R&amp;D in the United States&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2007&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in S&amp;E&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in S&amp;E&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3770,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 07-312&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Data from the 2005 Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (S&amp;E) show increased U.S. enrollment of first-time, full-time foreign graduate students in S&amp;E fields—the first increase since 2001—but a continuing decline in total enrollment of foreign S&amp;E graduate students. Overall enrollment and numbers of postdoctoral appointees in S&amp;E reached new peaks in 2005. Among major fields of study, enrollment declined most in computer sciences and engineering and increased most in psychology.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;02/06/2007&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/infbrief/nsf07312/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf07312&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2007.02.06&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Graduate Students and Postdoctorates in Science and Engineering (GSS)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;First-time S&amp;E Graduate Enrollment of Foreign Students Rebounds in 2005&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2007&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Academic R&amp;D Expenditures&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Academic R&amp;D Expenditures&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3768,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 07-311&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Data from the Survey of Research and Development Expenditures at Universities and Colleges show FY 2005 expenditures of $45.8 billion for R&amp;D in academic science and engineering, a 5.8% increase over FY 2004.