006&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Federal Funds for R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Funds for R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3642,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 06-313&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;The annual report, Federal Funds for Research and Development:  FY 2003-05, Detailed Statistical Tables consists of 131 tables derived from the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development, for Fiscal Years 2003-05, and from earlier surveys in this series.  These data provide data users with the most timely data possible and are not readily available from any other sources.   These statistical data tables will only be available via the World Wide Web.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;05/12/2006&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/nsf06313/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf06313&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2006.05.12&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Funds for Research and Development: Fiscal Years 2003-05&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2006&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3663,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 06-314&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report, Science and Engineering State Profiles: 2003-04, provides statistics on finances and personnel for the 50 States, Washington DC, and Puerto Rico with special emphasis on R&amp;D performance in 2003.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;05/08/2006&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/nsf06314/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf06314&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2006.05.08&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Research and Development Expenditures at Universities and Colleges&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Research and Development Expenditures at Universities and Colleges&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Science and Engineering State Profiles: 2003-04&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2006&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Academic R&amp;D Expenditures&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Academic R&amp;D Expenditures&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:3686,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 06-315&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Data from the Survey of Research and Development Expenditures at Universities and Colleges show industrial funding for R&amp;D in academic science and engineering dropped by 2.6 percent in FY 2004, continuing a decline that began in 2001. Expenditures overall increased by 7.2 percent over the previous year, fueled mostly by an increase in federal funding. Expenditures data are presented by source of funds, character of work, field, and leading institutions.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;04/28/2006&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/infbrief/nsf06315/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf06315&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2006.04.28&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Research and Development Expenditures at Universities and Colleges&quot;,&quot;Higher Education Research and Development (HERD) Survey&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quo