,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/30/2004&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/infbrief/nsf04337/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf04337&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2004.09.30&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal R&amp;D Funding Requests in FY 2005&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Facilities for S&amp;E Research&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Facilities for S&amp;E Research&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:1880,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 04-334&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;This report replaces Scientific and Engineering Research Facilities: 1999 (NSF 01-330) released in July 2001. SRS is releasing revised data for the 1999 cycle of Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities.  This survey provides data on the status of research facilities located at U.S. research-performing academic institutions and biomedical research organizations. The data was revised using new weights in order to provide national and subnational estimates.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/14/2004&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/nsf04334/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf04334&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2004.09.14&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Survey of Science and Engineering Research Facilities&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;S&amp;E Research Facilities: 1999&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[],&quot;id&quot;:1767,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 04-336&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Between 1988 and 2001 Latin American scientists nearly tripled their number of articles published in the world&#39;s most influential scientific and technical journals as well as their number of citations. Output for Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Costa Rica, Mexico, and Venezuela are examined and compared with emerging and developing countries in other world regions. Data are from the Institute for Scientific Information&#39;s Science and Social Science Citation Indexes.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;09/02/2004&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/infbrief/nsf04336/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf04336&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2004.09.02&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Latin America Shows Rapid Rise in S&amp;E Articles&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2004&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;Data Tables&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Federal Funds for R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Funds for R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:1865,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 04-335&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Detailed tables present data on federal obligations for research by federal agency and detailed field. Data are from annual surveys of federal funds for R&amp;D. Research funding levels from 11 agencies are shown by both basic and applied research, as well as the two combined. Data are actual for 1970 through 2001 and estimated for 2002 and 2003.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;08/12/2004&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/nsf04335/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf04335&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2004.08.12&quot;,&quot;survey&quo