elor’s or master’s degrees at U.S. institutions in academic years 1997 and 1998. Tables cover demographics (sex, race/ethnicity, citizenship); education (field, grade point average, sources of support, debt level); and employment (sector, primary work activity, salary). Data are collected directly from individuals through the National Survey of Recent College Graduates. The survey instrument appears at the end of the report.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;06/25/2003&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/nsf03319/&quot;,&quot;slugifiedNumber&quot;:&quot;nsf03319&quot;,&quot;sortDate&quot;:&quot;2003.06.25&quot;,&quot;survey&quot;:[&quot;National Survey of Recent College Graduates (NSRCG)&quot;],&quot;surveyDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;National Survey of Recent College Graduates (NSRCG)&quot;}],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Characteristics of Recent S&amp;E Graduates:1999&quot;,&quot;topics&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:&quot;2003&quot;},{&quot;aois&quot;:[],&quot;archived&quot;:true,&quot;contentType&quot;:&quot;InfoBrief&quot;,&quot;dataCollection&quot;:[&quot;Federal Funds for R&amp;D&quot;],&quot;dataCollectionDTO&quot;:[{&quot;active&quot;:false,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Federal Funds for R&amp;D&quot;}],&quot;id&quot;:1136,&quot;number&quot;:&quot;NSF 03-321&quot;,&quot;pubAbstract&quot;:&quot;Results from the Survey of Federal Funds for Research and Development project that Federal funding of R&amp;D and R&amp;D plant in FY 2003 will increase 6 percent over the FY 2002 level. Six Federal agencies account for 96 percent of total Federal R&amp;D funding, with the Department of Defense the largest contributor. Federal obligations for research by field show life sciences with the largest share, 54 percent, followed by engineering with 17 percent.&quot;,&quot;pubType&quot;:null,&quot;publishDate&quot;:&quot;06/20/2003&quot;,&quot;slug&quot;:&quot;https://www.nsf.gov/statistics/infbrief/nsf03321/